# {{ s.name }} — VFX

**Variant:** {{ variant }}

{{ s.description }}

## Setup

{% if variant == "particle_system" %}
1. Attach `{{ s.name }}` to a GameObject that has a **ParticleSystem** component (or assign one in the Inspector).
2. Call `Play()` / `Stop()` from any script, or enable **Play On Start**.
3. Set **Loop Effect** in the Inspector to keep the effect running continuously.
{% elif variant == "vfx_sequence" %}
1. Assign the **Effect Prefabs** array in the Inspector (one slot per sequence step).
2. Call `Play()` to run the full sequence, or enable **Play On Start**.
3. Sequence cues ({{ s.cues | length }} step(s)):
{% for cue in s.cues %}
   - Step {{ loop.index }}: `{{ cue.effect_id }}` at ({{ cue.x }}, {{ cue.y }}, {{ cue.z }}) scale {{ cue.scale }} after {{ cue.delay }}s
{% endfor %}
{% elif variant == "screen_fx" %}
1. Create a full-screen **UI Image** (stretch to fill the Canvas) and assign it to **Overlay**.
2. Optionally assign a **Flash Light** (directional or point) for the light spike.
3. Call `FadeIn()` / `FadeOut()` for screen transitions; `Flash()` for the light burst.
4. Fade color: RGB({{ s.fade_color_r }}, {{ s.fade_color_g }}, {{ s.fade_color_b }}) over {{ s.fade_duration }}s.
{% elif variant == "impact_fx" %}
1. Assign the **Effect Prefab** (a particle system prefab) in the Inspector.
2. Attach to any collider — particles spawn at the impact point when **{{ s.trigger_tag }}** objects collide.
3. Pool size: {{ s.pool_size }} — increase if many simultaneous impacts are expected.
{% endif %}
